\DOC MAYCHANGE_IDEMPOT_TAC

\TYPE {MAYCHANGE_IDEMPOT_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves goals asserting that a state-relation built by sequential composition of
change/assignment components absorbs a second copy of itself, closing the goal
outright.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. The goal's conclusion must be an equation between a
sequential composition {(u ,, u) ,, ...} — a parenthesised relation followed by
a repetition of the same component chain — and the single chain {u}. The tactic
then closes the goal:
{
   A ?- (u ,, u) ,, ... = u
   ===================================  MAYCHANGE_IDEMPOT_TAC
}
\noindent The assumptions {A} play no role.

\FAILURE
Fails, with an error arising from the relation-absorption conversion it relies
on, when the conclusion is an equation of this shape but the repeated
components are not in a form that conversion can absorb — for instance when the
composed chains, though syntactically similar, differ in some of their
components, or when the components are plain lambda-abstraction relations
rather than the structured change/assignment forms handled on the successful
goals.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces the only successful outcome is the one above, always
with the conclusion an equation of this self-absorbing composition form.

\ENDDOC
